error[E0083]: 'Outer' literal omits struct-typed field(s) 'b'
  --> error_struct_no_zero_value.bit:21:11
   |
21 |   let o = Outer{ a: 1 }
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a struct is a reference and has no zero value, so an omitted struct-typed field would be null rather than a zeroed body — give each one a value (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Outer' cannot be default-constructed: struct-typed field(s) 'b' have no zero value
  --> error_struct_no_zero_value.bit:25:7
   |
25 |   let p: Outer
   |       ^^^^^^^^ give the binding an initializer naming them, e.g. `= Outer{ ... }` (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Two' literal omits struct-typed field(s) 'first', 'second'
  --> error_struct_no_zero_value.bit:29:13
   |
29 |   let two = Two{ n: 1 }
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^ a struct is a reference and has no zero value, so an omitted struct-typed field would be null rather than a zeroed body — give each one a value (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Inner' literal omits struct-typed field(s) 'd'
  --> error_struct_no_zero_value.bit:33:30
   |
33 |   let deep = Outer{ a: 1, b: Inner{ xs: []u32(0) } }
   |                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a struct is a reference and has no zero value, so an omitted struct-typed field would be null rather than a zeroed body — give each one a value (§13.4)
